1. Purpose

This license is designed to be friendly to independent solo developers while
requiring separate permission for team, company, client, and organizational use.

2. Free Solo Developer Grant

Subject to the terms of this license, a Solo Developer is granted a free,
worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to:

- use this software;
- copy this software;
- modify this software;
- self-host and run this software; and
- create derivative works for their own use.

3. Who Qualifies as a Solo Developer

A "Solo Developer" means one natural person acting alone, for themselves, and
not on behalf of or for the benefit of any company, employer, client, agency,
studio, partnership, nonprofit, school, government body, online community, or
other organization.

You are not a Solo Developer if any of the following are true:

- more than one person has access to the source code, deployment, or admin
  control of the software;
- you are using the software for a team, business, startup, client, or other
  organization;
- you are building, operating, or customizing the software as part of paid work
  for someone else; or
- you are sharing modified or unmodified versions with collaborators,
  contractors, employees, or community staff.

4. Team, Company, Client, and Organizational Use

Any use that does not qualify as Solo Developer use requires prior written
permission from the copyright holder.

This includes, without limitation:

- internal team use;
- commercial company use;
- client work;
- agency or studio use;
- use by communities with multiple staff or contributors;
- use by schools, nonprofits, or government bodies; and
- any deployment, maintenance, or development involving more than one person.

If you want to use this software in those situations, you must obtain a
separate paid commercial or organizational license from the copyright holder.

5. Redistribution Restrictions

You may not sell, sublicense, rent, lease, distribute, publish, or provide this
software, in whole or in part, to any third party except with prior written
permission from the copyright holder.

You may not offer this software as a hosted service, template, boilerplate,
white-label product, SaaS, or managed platform for others except with prior
written permission from the copyright holder.

6. Attribution

You may keep this license file with the software. You may not remove copyright
notices from substantial portions of the software where they already exist.

7. Ownership

The software is licensed, not sold. All rights not expressly granted under this
license are reserved by the copyright holder.

8. Termination

Any violation of this license automatically terminates your rights under it.

Upon termination, you must stop using the software and delete or destroy all
